  },
  "question": {
    "text": "A block of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi></math> slides down the plane inclined at angle <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math> with an acceleration <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math> . The value of coefficient of kinetic friction will be :"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\st0057_7bf8273918ad.png\" style=\"width: 300px; height: 206px;\" /></p><p>Applying Newton&#39;s second law along the direction perpendicular to inlined plane:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>cos</mi><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>&nbsp;(As <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#952;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>30</mn><mo>&#176;</mo></math>)</p><p>(since the acceleration of block in the direction perpendicular to the inclined plane is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn></math>)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>cos</mi><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;.....(1)</p><p>Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi></math>&nbsp;be the coefficient of kinetic friction between the block and the inclined plane. Applying Newton&#39;s second law along inclined plane:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>sin</mi><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; ....(2)</p><p>(since the acceleration along the inclined plane,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>sin</mi><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mi>cos</mi><msup><mn>30</mn><mo>&#8728;</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math>&nbsp; &nbsp;(from equation 1 and 2)</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>-</mo><mfrac><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mi>&#956;</mi><mi>m</mi><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>m</mi><mfrac><mi>g</mi><mn>4</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo></math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>&#956;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac></math></p>"
  }
}